+ While a normal composer is running, its primary pointer action remains Stop when the draft is empty or input is unavailable. Actionable text or attachments switch the same seat to Queue Send; clearing or successfully submitting the draft restores Stop. The busy-Enter setting continues to select the Queue or Steer keyboard action. Continuable subagents keep separate Send and Stop actions ([decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/bug-fix/2026-08-20-running-draft-primary-send.md)).
+ 
++A plugin the composer cannot import contributes a keyboard gesture through `ctx.conversation.composerKeys`: handlers are consulted in ascending `order`, then registration order, from a bubbling listener on the composer card, so the editor, the trigger menus, and the bar's own keymap see the gesture first and one they consumed arrives with `defaultPrevented` set. Each handler receives the live draft, the caret projection the caret indexes into, the IME-composition flag, editability, Session identity, and the public `InputActions` face; `'handled'` consumes the gesture. The bar is the resident `session-maybe` entry, so a handler covers the composer in every state it is on screen, the blank-Session Hero included — where the Session-scoped docks are suppressed ([decision](../../../.agents/notes/proposed/feature/2026-10-11-client-composer-key-handlers.md)).
